`walk`: `after` is "dd/x", which is not under "d": it is a path an earlier walk of it returned
`walk`: `after` is "e", which is not under "d": it is a path an earlier walk of it returned
`walk`: a depth of 0: 1 is the folder's own entries
`walk`: a kind of "link": "file", "directory" or "other"
`walk` takes `depth`, `like`, `kind`, `skip`, `after` and `keep_reads`, not `nope`
`walk`: `keep_reads` of -1: it is a count of reads
`walk`: its depth must be an integer, not a string
`walk` takes a map, given a list (`#l` is a list's length)
`walk("a.txt")`: a part of the path is a file, not a folder (NotDir): `is_dir(p)` asks first
`walk("nope")`: not found (FileNotFound): `exists(p)` asks first
